    "original_goal": "Resolve whether the UAC v1.0.0-final spec's Knowledge Reconciliation Engine should be modeled as Stage 0.5 (a sequential pipeline stage with one input/output boundary, running once per compile) or as Cross-Cutting System 10 (an always-available service every stage can call continuously). The frozen spec explicitly flags this as unresolved: the source material places it in both locations. Research how comparable systems make this same architectural choice \u2014 ETL/data-quality reconciliation engines, compiler constraint or attribute-grammar passes, workflow-orchestration conflict-resolution patterns \u2014 and recommend which model fits UAC's actual need: resolving conflicting sourced claims (source contradiction, jurisdictional/context variance, qualified consensus) between Knowledge Acquisition (Stage 0) and Domain Intelligence (Stage 1).",
